{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function injectHotkey(\n   hotkey, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/angular-hotkeys/src/injectHotkey.ts#L85","children":[{"type":"text","value":"injectHotkey.ts:85"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular inject-based API for registering a keyboard hotkey."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses the singleton HotkeyManager for efficient event handling.\nThe callback receives both the keyboard event and a context object\ncontaining the hotkey string and parsed hotkey."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call in an injection context (e.g. constructor or field initializer).\nUses effect() to track reactive dependencies and update registration\nwhen options or the callback change.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled: false"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the registration (visible in devtools) and only suppresses firing; the same\nhandle is updated instead of unregistering and re-registering when identity is unchanged."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hotkey","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hotkey"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RegisterableHotkey"},{"type":"text","value":" | (() => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RegisterableHotkey"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hotkey string (e.g. 'Mod+S', 'Escape') or getter function"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyCallback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function to call when the hotkey is pressed"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"| "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/InjectHotkeyOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InjectHotkeyOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n| (() => "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/InjectHotkeyOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InjectHotkeyOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options for the hotkey behavior, or getter for reactive options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"@Component({ ... })\nexport class SaveButtonComponent {\n  private readonly saveCount = signal(0)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+S', (event, { hotkey }) => {\n      event.preventDefault()\n      this.saveCount.update(c => c + 1)\n    })\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"@Component({ ... })\nexport class ModalComponent {\n  isOpen = signal(true)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Escape', () => this.close(), () => ({ enabled: this.isOpen() }))\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"@Component({ ... })\nexport class EditorComponent {\n  private readonly editorRef = viewChild<ElementRef<HTMLDivElement>>('editorRef')\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+B', () => this.toggleBold(), () => ({\n      target: this.editorRef()?.nativeElement ?? null,\n    }))\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"hotkey","text":"hotkey","level":3},{"id":"callback","text":"callback","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction injectHotkey(\n   hotkey, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [injectHotkey.ts:85](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/angular-hotkeys/src/injectHotkey.ts#L85)\n\nAngular inject-based API for registering a keyboard hotkey.\n\nUses the singleton HotkeyManager for efficient event handling.\nThe callback receives both the keyboard event and a context object\ncontaining the hotkey string and parsed hotkey.\n\nCall in an injection context (e.g. constructor or field initializer).\nUses effect() to track reactive dependencies and update registration\nwhen options or the callback change.\n`enabled: false` keeps the registration (visible in devtools) and only suppresses firing; the same\nhandle is updated instead of unregistering and re-registering when identity is unchanged.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkey\n\n`RegisterableHotkey` \\| (() => `RegisterableHotkey`)\n\nThe hotkey string (e.g. 'Mod+S', 'Escape') or getter function\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nThe function to call when the hotkey is pressed\n\n### options?\n\n  \\| [`InjectHotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/InjectHotkeyOptions.md)\n  \\| (() => [`InjectHotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/InjectHotkeyOptions.md))\n\nOptions for the hotkey behavior, or getter for reactive options\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\n@Component({ ... })\nexport class SaveButtonComponent {\n  private readonly saveCount = signal(0)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+S', (event, { hotkey }) => {\n      event.preventDefault()\n      this.saveCount.update(c => c + 1)\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```ts\n@Component({ ... })\nexport class ModalComponent {\n  isOpen = signal(true)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Escape', () => this.close(), () => ({ enabled: this.isOpen() }))\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```ts\n@Component({ ... })\nexport class EditorComponent {\n  private readonly editorRef = viewChild<ElementRef<HTMLDivElement>>('editorRef')\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+B', () => this.toggleBold(), () => ({\n      target: this.editorRef()?.nativeElement ?? null,\n    }))\n  }\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: injectHotkey\ntitle: injectHotkey\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction injectHotkey(\n   hotkey, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [injectHotkey.ts:85](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/angular-hotkeys/src/injectHotkey.ts#L85)\n\nAngular inject-based API for registering a keyboard hotkey.\n\nUses the singleton HotkeyManager for efficient event handling.\nThe callback receives both the keyboard event and a context object\ncontaining the hotkey string and parsed hotkey.\n\nCall in an injection context (e.g. constructor or field initializer).\nUses effect() to track reactive dependencies and update registration\nwhen options or the callback change.\n`enabled: false` keeps the registration (visible in devtools) and only suppresses firing; the same\nhandle is updated instead of unregistering and re-registering when identity is unchanged.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkey\n\n`RegisterableHotkey` \\| (() => `RegisterableHotkey`)\n\nThe hotkey string (e.g. 'Mod+S', 'Escape') or getter function\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nThe function to call when the hotkey is pressed\n\n### options?\n\n  \\| [`InjectHotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/InjectHotkeyOptions.md)\n  \\| (() => [`InjectHotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/InjectHotkeyOptions.md))\n\nOptions for the hotkey behavior, or getter for reactive options\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\n@Component({ ... })\nexport class SaveButtonComponent {\n  private readonly saveCount = signal(0)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+S', (event, { hotkey }) => {\n      event.preventDefault()\n      this.saveCount.update(c => c + 1)\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```ts\n@Component({ ... })\nexport class ModalComponent {\n  isOpen = signal(true)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Escape', () => this.close(), () => ({ enabled: this.isOpen() }))\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```ts\n@Component({ ... })\nexport class EditorComponent {\n  private readonly editorRef = viewChild<ElementRef<HTMLDivElement>>('editorRef')\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+B', () => this.toggleBold(), () => ({\n      target: this.editorRef()?.nativeElement ?? null,\n    }))\n  }\n}\n```\n"}
